#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "Understand open-shell versus closed-shell options and the effect on subspace construction for the latest version of Sample-based quantum diagonalization (SQD)"
msgstr "Pahami opsi open-shell versus closed-shell dan pengaruhnya terhadap konstruksi subruang untuk versi terbaru Sample-based quantum diagonalization (SQD)"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Understand open-shell versus closed-shell options and the effect on subspace construction"
msgstr "Pahami opsi open-shell versus closed-shell dan pengaruhnya terhadap konstruksi subruang"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<OpenInLabBanner notebookPath=\"addons/qiskit-addon-sqd/guides/select-open-closed-shell.ipynb\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this guide, we will show how to choose subspace dimensions in the `qiskit_addon_sqd` package to post-process quantum samples using the [self-consistent configuration recovery technique](https://arxiv.org/abs/2405.05068).\n"
msgstr "Di panduan ini, kita akan tunjukkan cara memilih dimensi subruang di paket `qiskit_addon_sqd` untuk pasca-proses sampel kuantum memakai [teknik pemulihan konfigurasi self-consistent](https://arxiv.org/abs/2405.05068).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "More importantly, this guide also highlights some differences in the behavior in the subspace construction when run in `open_shell = False` or `open_shell = True` modes:\n"
msgstr "Yang lebih penting, panduan ini juga menyoroti beberapa perbedaan perilaku konstruksi subruang saat dijalankan dalam mode `open_shell = False` atau `open_shell = True`:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`open_shell = False` only works when the number of spin-up and spin-down electrons is the same.\n"
msgstr "`open_shell = False` hanya bekerja jika jumlah elektron spin-up dan spin-down sama.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`open_shell = True` must be used when the number of spin-up and spin-down electrons is different. It can also be used when the number of spin-up and spin-down electrons is the same. However, in this last case, there is a difference in the sizes of the subspaces generated between `open_shell = False` and `open_shell = True`, as discussed in this guide.\n"
msgstr "`open_shell = True` harus dipakai jika jumlah elektron spin-up dan spin-down berbeda. Mode ini juga bisa dipakai jika jumlah elektron spin-up dan spin-down sama. Namun, pada kasus terakhir ini, ukuran subruang yang dihasilkan berbeda antara `open_shell = False` dan `open_shell = True`, seperti dibahas di panduan ini.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**NOTE:** Some of the electronic-configuration (bitstring) manipulations in this package have as a goal to preserve the total spin symmetry $S^2$. Standard Selected Configuration Interaction (SCI) solvers cannot impose $S^2$ conservation exactly. Consequently, they do so approximately via a Lagrange multiplier.\n"
msgstr "**CATATAN:** Beberapa manipulasi konfigurasi elektronik (bitstring) di paket ini bertujuan menjaga simetri spin total $S^2$. Solver Selected Configuration Interaction (SCI) standar tidak bisa memaksakan kekekalan $S^2$ secara eksak. Akibatnya, mereka melakukannya secara aproksimasi lewat pengali Lagrange.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The choice of electronic configurations entering the eigenstate solver can also have a strong effect in the conservation of spin. For example, in a (2-electron, 2-orbital) system, one can sample the configuration $|1001\\rangle$ (having a single spin-up excitation over the RHF state $|0101\\rangle$), which is a linear combination of the open-shell singlet and triplet states, respectively $(|1001\\rangle ± |0110\\rangle) /\\sqrt{2}$. If the configuration |0110⟩ is not sampled, one can construct neither eigenfunction of total spin, leading to spin contamination or redundancy (the configuration |1001⟩ is involved in a CI calculation, but has coefficient 0 in the CI vector). Given that a single sample $|1001\\rangle$ is generated in the quantum computer, this is how the `sqd` package handles this situation:\n"
msgstr "Pilihan konfigurasi elektronik yang masuk ke eigenstate solver juga bisa sangat memengaruhi kekekalan spin. Misalnya, pada sistem (2 elektron, 2 orbital), kita bisa mensampel konfigurasi $|1001\\rangle$ (yang punya satu eksitasi spin-up dari keadaan RHF $|0101\\rangle$), yang merupakan kombinasi linear dari keadaan singlet dan triplet open-shell, masing-masing $(|1001\\rangle ± |0110\\rangle) /\\sqrt{2}$. Jika konfigurasi |0110⟩ tidak disampel, kita tidak bisa membangun eigenfunction spin total mana pun, sehingga terjadi kontaminasi spin atau redundansi (konfigurasi |1001⟩ ikut dalam perhitungan CI, tetapi punya koefisien 0 di vektor CI). Jika hanya satu sampel $|1001\\rangle$ yang dihasilkan di komputer kuantum, beginilah cara paket `sqd` menangani situasi ini:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`open_shell = False`:\n"
msgstr "`open_shell = False`:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '    1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The $1001$ bitstring is split in half, representing spin-up and spin-down configurations: $10$ (up) and $01$ (down).\n"
msgstr "Bitstring $1001$ dibelah dua, mewakili konfigurasi spin-up dan spin-down: $10$ (up) dan $01$ (down).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '    2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The list of unique spin-polarized configurations is constructed: $\\mathcal{U} = [01, 10]$.\n"
msgstr "Daftar konfigurasi terpolarisasi-spin yang unik dibentuk: $\\mathcal{U} = [01, 10]$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '    3. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "We then consider all possible combinations of $\\mathcal{U}$ elements to form the basis: $\\left \\{ |0101\\rangle, |0110\\rangle , |1001\\rangle , |1010\\rangle \\right \\}$, which contains the singlet and triplet states.\n"
msgstr "Lalu kita pertimbangkan semua kombinasi yang mungkin dari elemen $\\mathcal{U}$ untuk membentuk basis: $\\left \\{ |0101\\rangle, |0110\\rangle , |1001\\rangle , |1010\\rangle \\right \\}$, yang memuat keadaan singlet dan triplet.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`open_shell = True`:\n"
msgstr "`open_shell = True`:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '    1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Contrary to the `open_shell = False` case, we do not combine the halves of the bitstring to form the basis.\n"
msgstr "Berbeda dengan kasus `open_shell = False`, kita tidak menggabungkan kedua belahan bitstring untuk membentuk basis.\n"

