msgstr "Kulit tertutup {#closed-shell}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This example shows how the bitstrings are manipulated in a (2-electron, 4-orbital) system.\n"
msgstr "Contoh ini menunjukkan cara bitstring dimanipulasi pada sistem (2 elektron, 4 orbital).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Specify by hand a dictionary of measurement outcomes:\n"
msgstr "Tentukan secara manual sebuah dictionary berisi hasil pengukuran:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Transform the counts `dict` into a bitstring matrix and probability array for post-processing:\n"
msgstr "Ubah `dict` counts menjadi matriks bitstring dan array probabilitas untuk pasca-proses:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Subsample a single batch of size two:\n"
msgstr "Subsampling satu batch berukuran dua:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "``n_batches = 1``: Number of batches of configurations used by the different calls to the eigenstate solver\n"
msgstr "``n_batches = 1``: Jumlah batch konfigurasi yang dipakai oleh berbagai panggilan ke eigenstate solver\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "``samples_per_batch = 2``: Number of unique configurations to include in each batch\n"
msgstr "``samples_per_batch = 2``: Jumlah konfigurasi unik yang disertakan di setiap batch\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Obtain decimal representation of the spin-up and spin-down bitstrings used by the eigenstate solver.\n"
msgstr "Dapatkan representasi desimal dari bitstring spin-up dan spin-down yang dipakai oleh eigenstate solver.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The first element in the tuple corresponds to the decimal representation of the spin-up configurations, while the second element in the tuple corresponds to the decimal representation of the spin-down configurations:\n"
msgstr "Elemen pertama dalam tuple sesuai dengan representasi desimal dari konfigurasi spin-up, sedangkan elemen kedua dalam tuple sesuai dengan representasi desimal dari konfigurasi spin-down:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Note that while the number of samples per batch is two, and the sampled bitstrings are: $00010010$ and $01001000$, four electronic configurations are generated per spin-species. In this case, the set of unique spin-polarized configurations is given by:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{U} = \\{ 0001, 0010, 0100, 1000 \\}\n"
"$$\n"
"whose base-10 decimal representation is\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{U}_{10} = \\{ 1, 2, 4, 8 \\}\n"
"$$\n"
"Basis of the subspace:\n"
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan bahwa meski jumlah sampel per batch adalah dua, dan bitstring yang disampel adalah $00010010$ dan $01001000$, empat konfigurasi elektronik dihasilkan per spesies spin. Dalam kasus ini, himpunan konfigurasi terpolarisasi-spin yang unik adalah:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{U} = \\{ 0001, 0010, 0100, 1000 \\}\n"
"$$\n"
"dengan representasi desimal basis-10\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{U}_{10} = \\{ 1, 2, 4, 8 \\}\n"
"$$\n"
"Basis dari subruang:\n"

